			[ 'Who has to prove the property was left dirty in a deposit dispute?', 'The landlord, because the deposit belongs to the tenant. They need evidence such as the check-in inventory, check-out report and photos showing the property was returned in a worse condition than at the start, beyond fair wear and tear.' ],
			[ 'Can a landlord deduct cleaning costs without a check-in inventory?', 'They can propose a deduction, but without a check-in inventory it is very difficult to prove the property was cleaner at the start. That makes it hard for a landlord to win a cleaning claim at adjudication.' ],
