		'excerpt'     => 'How landlords and agents can plan void cleans so empty rentals are ready for viewings and new tenants sooner, with a full void cleaning checklist.',
		'content'     => <<<'HTML'
<p>Void property cleaning is the clean carried out while a rental is empty between tenancies, bringing it up to the standard that will be recorded on the next check-in inventory. To turn a property around faster, book the clean as soon as you know the check-out date, finish repairs and decorating first, and make cleaning the last job before photos, viewings and the new check-in.</p>
<p>Every week a property sits empty means lost rent, and usually council tax and bills in the landlord's name. Cleaning is one of the simplest parts of a void to get right, and one of the easiest to let slip, because it depends on everyone else finishing on time.</p>
<p>Our team handles void cleans for landlords and letting agents across Hull and East Yorkshire, from single terraces to larger portfolios. Here is how to plan them so the next tenant moves in sooner.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Clean last: after repairs, decorating and carpet fitting, but before photos and viewings.</li><li>Book cleaners as soon as you know the check-out date, not when the trades finish.</li><li>Use the next check-in inventory as your cleaning standard, so the new tenancy starts with a clear benchmark.</li><li>Keep an empty property aired and checked so dust, damp and pests don't build up while it is vacant.</li></ul></div>
<h2>What is void property cleaning?</h2>
<p>"Void" is the letting industry's term for the period when a rental has no tenant. A void clean overlaps with an end of tenancy clean but isn't quite the same thing. The outgoing tenant may or may not have cleaned, the check-out may have flagged problems, and repairs or decorating may have left dust and debris behind.</p>
<p>The aim of a void clean is simple: get the property to a standard you are happy to photograph, show to applicants and record on a fresh inventory. Our <a href="{{service:end-of-tenancy-cleaning}}">end of tenancy cleaning service</a> is often booked for exactly this, following the same detailed <a href="{{guide:end-of-tenancy-cleaning-checklist}}">room-by-room end of tenancy checklist</a> letting agents use.</p>
<h2>Why cleaning holds up void turnarounds</h2>
<p>Cleaning itself rarely takes long. Delays usually come from how it fits around everything else:</p>
<ul>
<li>The clean is booked late, once the trades are finished, and the first free slot is days away.</li>
<li>Decorators or a plumber come in after the clean and leave dust, footprints or paint splashes.</li>
<li>The outgoing tenant's own clean wasn't up to standard, but nobody checked until a viewing.</li>
<li>Keys are with the agent, a contractor or the outgoing tenant, and access takes days to arrange.</li>
<li>Nobody inspects the property between the clean and the first viewing.</li>
</ul>
<h2>The right order of work for a void property</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check-out inspection.</strong> Compare the property with the check-in inventory and take photos before anything else happens.</li>
<li><strong>Clearance.</strong> Remove belongings, rubbish and anything left in the loft, shed or garden.</li>
<li><strong>Repairs and safety checks.</strong> Plumbing, electrics, gas safety and any other legal checks due.</li>
<li><strong>Decorating.</strong> Touch-ups or full redecoration, with time for paint to dry.</li>
<li><strong>Carpets.</strong> New carpets fitted, or existing ones deep cleaned.</li>
<li><strong>The clean.</strong> A full top-to-bottom clean of the empty property.</li>
<li><strong>Final check and photos.</strong> Walk round, then take marketing photos while it looks its best.</li>
<li><strong>New check-in inventory.</strong> Record the condition, ideally straight after the clean.</li>
</ol>
<p>Where a void involves more than touch-ups, such as a new kitchen or replastering, fine dust settles everywhere for days. An <a href="{{service:after-builders-cleaning}}">after builders clean</a> deals with that properly, and our guide to <a href="{{guide:removing-paint-and-plaster-dust}}">removing plaster dust and paint splashes</a> explains why ordinary cleaning struggles with it. Carpets that are staying can be refreshed with our <a href="{{service:carpet-upholstery-cleaning}}">hot water extraction carpet cleaning</a> before the final clean.</p>
<h2>Void property cleaning checklist</h2>
<h3>Kitchen</h3>
<ul>
<li>Oven, hob, grill and extractor hood and filter degreased</li>
<li>Fridge and freezer defrosted, cleaned and left with doors ajar if switched off</li>
<li>Cupboards and drawers emptied and wiped inside and out</li>
<li>Worktops, splashbacks, tiles and grout cleaned</li>
<li>Sink and taps descaled, plughole cleaned</li>
<li>Washing machine seal and drawer cleaned</li>
</ul>
<h3>Bathrooms</h3>
<ul>
<li>Toilet cleaned inside and out, including the base and behind</li>
<li>Bath, shower tray, screen and tiles descaled</li>
<li>Sealant checked for mould and replaced if needed</li>
<li>Extractor fan cover cleaned, mirrors and cabinets polished</li>
</ul>
<h3>Throughout</h3>
<ul>
<li>Light fittings, switches, sockets and door handles</li>
<li>Skirting boards, door frames, radiators and window sills</li>
<li>Windows inside, plus tracks and frames</li>
<li>Wardrobes and built-in storage wiped out</li>
<li>Carpets hoovered and hard floors mopped</li>
</ul>
<h3>Outside</h3>
<ul>
<li>Bins emptied and washed</li>
<li>Paths swept and front door and letterbox cleaned</li>
<li>Garden, shed and garage cleared of rubbish</li>
</ul>
<h2>Keeping an empty property clean while it's vacant</h2>
<p>A property can go downhill quickly when nobody is living in it, especially through the winter. If a void is likely to last more than a couple of weeks:</p>
<ul>
<li>Visit regularly, and open windows for a while to air the rooms.</li>
<li>Keep the heating on low in cold weather to protect against frost and condensation.</li>
<li>Run the taps and flush the toilets on each visit so water doesn't sit in the pipes.</li>
<li>Clear post and junk mail, which advertises an empty property.</li>
<li>Check for mould on walls, ceilings and window reveals.</li>
<li>Look for signs of pests, particularly in kitchens and around bins.</li>
</ul>
<p>Older terraces and coastal properties in places like <a href="{{area:bridlington}}">Bridlington</a> are particularly prone to damp when they are unheated. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:damp-and-mould-in-older-homes}}">condensation, damp and black mould</a> explains what to look for. A quick refresh clean just before the new tenant moves in deals with any dust that has settled since the main clean.</p>
<h2>How to cut void time with better cleaning arrangements</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Have a standing arrangement</strong> with one cleaning company, so a void clean is a phone call rather than a search.</li>
<li><strong>Use key holding</strong> so cleaners can get in without waiting for someone to meet them.</li>
<li><strong>Know how long it takes.</strong> Our guide to <a href="{{guide:how-long-does-end-of-tenancy-cleaning-take}}">how long an end of tenancy clean takes</a> helps you plan the gap between trades and viewings.</li>
<li><strong>Ask for photos</strong> after the clean, so you can see the result without a site visit.</li>
<li><strong>Use weekends.</strong> We work seven days a week, so a Friday check-out can be cleaned before Monday viewings.</li>
<li><strong>Record the result.</strong> Our guide to <a href="{{guide:landlord-inventory-cleaning-standards}}">recording cleanliness at check-in</a> shows how to turn a fresh clean into a solid inventory benchmark.</li>
</ul>
<div class="cc-callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Book the void clean provisionally on the day you receive the tenant's notice. You can always move the date, but it is much harder to find a slot at short notice around month-end.</p></div>
<h2>Void cleaning for landlords and letting agents</h2>
<p>Our <a href="{{service:end-of-tenancy-cleaning}}">end of tenancy and void cleaning</a> follows letting-agent and inventory checklists, with DBS-checked, insured cleaners who bring their own equipment. We agree a fixed quote before work starts, invoice landlords and agents directly, and come back to re-clean anything that isn't right.</p>
<p>We cover rentals across the region, including <a href="{{local:end-of-tenancy-cleaning-hull}}">end of tenancy cleaning in Hull</a>. Our <a href="{{page:landlords}}">landlord services page</a> explains how we support portfolios, or send us the address and check-out date through our <a href="{{page:contact}}">contact page</a>.</p>
